  "asr_text": "The researchers used X-rays to study the shape of the protein inside the crystals. Fats were bound to the protein, and sugars were attached too. If you were expecting a fancy latte, what you got was a map of molecules. Suddenly, we're in a science lab. And the paper includes a striking estimate: the crystals contain more than three times as much energy as the same weight of milk from several kinds of mammals, the final boss of nutrition. At this point, the marketing team might be ready to leap into action. But hold on. The comparison was between crystals and milk. It does not mean that drinking them would make people three times as energetic. Take that number on its own, and before you know it, a science story can turn into a TV shopping show.",
